// The framework's own connect point for monitoring. Every service in a project consumes
// it and the monitor owns it, so events reach the monitor over an ordinary mesh link:
// mutual TLS, the same deny-by-default consumer list as anything else, and a `Caller`
// whose `entity` is the certificate subject. That last part is what makes the record
// trustworthy. An entity cannot report events as another entity, because it cannot present
// another entity's certificate.
//
// A client never consumes this. A browser cannot reach the mesh, and a value a visitor
// controls must never be read as an entity identity (docs/security.md, the two identity
// systems). What a browser does reaches the record through the edge that served it, as
// something observed rather than something claimed.

contract Ingest {
    // One batch of events, each a serialized TraceEvent. Bounded at the boundary rather
    // than trusted: 512 events is a large batch and an unbounded list is a way to make the
    // monitor allocate whatever a broken or hostile entity feels like sending.
    slot publish(list[512] events)

    // Still here, and what it last saw. An entity that stops sending is the case a monitor
    // exists to notice, and silence is indistinguishable from health without this.
    slot heartbeat(string[64] entity, double sentMs)
}
